:: Church encounter - holy comfort [bg-guesthouse]
<h1 class="ptitle">GUEST HOUSE</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A kind nun sits with the unhappiest guest in the house. If the guest leans on xanax, whippits or drink, they say so. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Guest house'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun, _guest = _cast.guest>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun), _gName = setup.displayName(_guest)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _gHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_guest), _gHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_guest), _gHim = setup.pronounceWho(_guest)>>
/* Compassion was already worth +2 here before the trait table; byNun gives +1 of it, _bonus keeps the other */
<<set _bonus = setup.personality.has(_nun, 'compassionate') ? 1 : 0>>
<<set _vice = _ce.vice(_guest)>>
<<set _viceName = _vice ? _ce.itemName(_vice).toLowerCase() : ''>>
<<set _viceWords = { xanax: 'the pills', whippit: 'the whippits', alcohol: 'the bottle' }>>
<<set _gMc = setup.npc.mcName(_guest), _nMc = setup.npc.mcName(_nun)>>

In a quiet corner of the dormitory, <<=_gName>> sits hunched on the edge of a bed with <<=_gHis>> face in <<=_gHis>> hands. <<=_nunName>> sits beside <<=_gHim>>, close enough that their shoulders touch, saying nothing for the moment and simply staying.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _guest>>
	I don't even know what's wrong. Nothing happened. I just wake up and it's all so heavy, every day, and I can't put it down.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<sayNpc _nun>>
	You don't have to know what it is. The holy texts say grief doesn't always have a name, and the faithful are told to sit with it anyway. So I'm sitting with you.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<if _vice>>
	<<=_gName>> laughs, small and unhappy.
	<br /><br />
	<<sayNpc _guest>>
		I keep reaching for <<=_viceWords[_vice]>>. It helps for a while, and then it doesn't, and then I need more of it. I think I'm leaning on it too much. I don't know what else to lean on.
	<</sayNpc>>
	<br />
<</if>>
<<=_nunName>> looks up and sees you. <<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> doesn't ask for anything, but <<=_nHe>> doesn't look away either. <<=_gName>> follows <<=_nHis>> gaze and scrubs hastily at <<=_gHis>> eyes.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _guest>>
	Oh. <<=ucfirst(_gMc)>>. I didn't want you to see me like this.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<if _vice>>
		<<set _giftLabel = "Give " + _gHim + " some " + _viceName + " and tell " + _gHim + " it's okay to lean on it">>
		<<if setup.cabinInventory.has(_vice)>>
			<<link _giftLabel>>
				<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
					<<addmins 5>>
					<<run setup.cabinInventory.to_npc(_guest, _vice)>>
					<<run _fx.change(_guest, 'happy', 2, 3)>>
					You crouch down in front of <<=_gName>> and press the <<=_viceName>> into <<=_gHis>> hands.
					<br /><br />
					<<you>>
						This is the end of the world. Nobody gets through it without a crutch. If this one helps, use it, and don't let anyone make you feel bad about it.
					<</you>>
					<br />
					<<=_gName>> closes <<=_gHis>> fingers around it and some of the tightness goes out of <<=_gHis>> shoulders.
					<br /><br />
					<<sayNpc _guest>>
						Thank you, <<=_gMc>>.
					<</sayNpc>>
					<br /> <<=_nunName>> watches you with an expression you can't quite read, then rests a hand on <<=_gName>>'s back.
					<br /><br />
					<<sayNpc _nun>>
						Just remember it isn't the only thing holding you up. I'm here too. Come and find me, before you go looking for that.
					<</sayNpc>>
					<br />
					[[Continue|Guest house]]
					<<nurseryEffects>>
				<</replace>>
			<</link>>
		<<else>>
			<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc">
				<<=_giftLabel>> (you have none)
			</div>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _helpLabel = 'Sit with them and help lift ' + _gHis + ' spirits (Uses 30 minutes)'>>
	<<link _helpLabel>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 30>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _guest, 'happy', 4 + _bonus, 8 + _bonus)>>
			You sit down on the other side of <<=_gName>>. For a while you just talk about nothing: the weather, the garden, the dog that keeps stealing boots from the porch. Then, when <<=_gHe>> is ready, you talk about the heavy things too.
			<br /><br />
			<<=_nunName>> knows when to speak and when to let a silence do the work, and you find yourself following <<=_nHis>> lead. You remind <<=_gName>> of things <<=_gHe>> has done here that mattered, people who would miss <<=_gHim>>, small proofs that <<=_gHe>> is not just surviving but needed.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _guest>>
				I didn't think anyone noticed any of that, <<=_gMc>>.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<sayNpc _nun>>
				We notice. That's what we're for.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			By the time you get up to leave, <<=_gName>> has stopped hiding <<=_gHis>> face, and something like a smile is trying its luck at the corners of <<=_gHis>> mouth.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Guest house]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Leave them to it'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _guest, 'happy', 1 + _bonus, 2 + _bonus)>>
			<<sayNpc _nun>>
				Go on, <<=_nMc>>. I'll stay with <<=_gHim>>.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			You leave them in peace. Behind you, <<=_nunName>> starts to hum something soft and old, and after a while <<=_gName>> leans <<=_gHis>> head against <<=_nHis>> shoulder.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Guest house]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
